# Export list for Mpv.framework (Apple ld64 `-exported_symbols_list`).
#
# The Mach-O counterpart of the Android fork's `include/mpv.ver` version script.
# mpv's waf build derived a version script from libmpv/mpv.def, which is why the
# v0.7.2 binaries exported exactly the 53 names in that file. mpv 0.37 deleted
# mpv.def and 0.41's meson relies solely on `gnu_symbol_visibility: 'hidden'`
# plus MPV_EXPORT in the public headers. That governs mpv's OWN objects and does
# nothing whatsoever for the archives linked into it.
#
# On this fork that used to be harmless -- FFmpeg and mbedTLS ship as separate
# dylibs here, so nothing static entered the link. mpv 0.41 changed that:
# libplacebo is mandatory (see nix/packages/mk-pkg-libplacebo) and is linked
# statically, and every one of its ~570 public symbols is decorated
# `PL_API __attribute__((visibility("default")))` on non-Windows targets
# regardless of PL_STATIC (src/include/libplacebo/config.h.in:71). Without this
# file they all land in Mpv.framework's export table.
#
# Not cosmetic: a React Native app routinely loads other media libraries, and a
# leaked symbol set makes the dynamic linker's choice of whose implementation a
# call binds to essentially arbitrary -- the exact class of collision this
# project chose libmpv to avoid.
#
# The list is exact rather than an `_mpv_*` wildcard so that a new export is a
# review event and the count is assertable against the shipped dylib: 54 names,
# every one of them declared MPV_EXPORT in include/mpv/{client,render,render_gl,
# stream_cb}.h of mpv 0.41.0. v0.7.2 (mpv 0.36) shipped 53; the single addition
# is `mpv_get_time_ns`.
_mpv_abort_async_command
_mpv_client_api_version
_mpv_client_id
_mpv_client_name
_mpv_command
_mpv_command_async
_mpv_command_node
_mpv_command_node_async
_mpv_command_ret
_mpv_command_string
_mpv_create
_mpv_create_client
_mpv_create_weak_client
